issue.body:
Header `system.h` gets installed along with `dronecore.h` and plugin header files.
DroneCore apps do:

```cpp
System &system = dc.system();
...
// have access to entire System interface
```

This implies, we're letting applications access to `System` interface as well. In other words, _applications can even compose MAVLink messages and send it across!_
I think thats not right. We may decide to export minimal interface like, `has_camera(1)`, `has_gimbal()`, etc;

As I understand, we insist DroneCore apps to use plugins rather than `System` interface. Please correct me.

On the other hand, `System` interface is needed for plugins. So, one possible way is to expose:

```cpp
class MAVLinkSystem {
// Current Device contents which are required by plugins goes here.
};
```

to plugins.
**Note:**_I chose name `MAVLinkSystem` here because its internal to DroneCore and not exposed to public. I am fine with any suitable name that makes sense._

For DroneCore applications, lets provide 

```cpp
class System {
// Minimal interface needed for DroneCore apps
};
```

Kindly share your thoughts.
